fix: re-stage secrets + wait for running state on sandbox resume

start_sandbox now:
1. Waits for the Apple container to reach "running" state after
   `container start` returns (polls up to 15s) to prevent the
   gateway from seeing a stale "stopped" snapshot during the
   brief window before the VM resumes.
2. Cleans the stale secret staging directory before re-writing
   auth materials (write_owner_only_file uses create_new(true)
   which fails on existing files).
3. Re-stages auth bundle + backend descriptor + TLS certs with
   the gateway's fresh launch_authentication (new generation_id,
   new JWT) before re-spawning the host supervisor.

stop_sandbox now terminates the host supervisor before stopping
the container, so start_sandbox can cleanly re-spawn it.

E2E verified: create → Ready → exec → stop all pass.
Resume (start) reaches Starting but does not transition to Ready
because the boundary inside the VM gets a new random port on
container restart while the supervisor's backend descriptor still
points at the old port.  Fixing resume requires a stable boundary
port across restarts — deferred as a known limitation.
